BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:REAL TIME REVOLUTION®: “Lodging as the Nature of the Campaign W
 ill Admit”
DTSTART:20260920T093000
DTEND:20260920T170000
DTSTAMP:20260920T144436Z
UID:0269d513ea5e51de991c774dbbc8fb@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Watch soldiers of the Northern Continental Army build huts at 
 Ticonderoga\, just as they did 250 years ago atop Liberty Hill. See Americ
 an ingenuity in action as soldiers use boards posts\, and beams to build n
 ew shelter as they guard Ticonderoga into the fall. Discover the historian
 s’ detective work\, piecing together this unique housing of 1776\, as so
 ldiers prepared to halt the inevitable British attack. This event is made 
 possible\, in part\, thanks to a Preserving America Grant from Americana C
 orner. “Lodging as the Nature of the Campaign will Admit” programming 
 is included in your General Admission ticket! Tickets are valid for two co
 nsecutive days.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fort Ticonderoga\, 102 Fort Ti Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/real-time-
 revolution-lodging-as-the-nature-of-the-campaign-will-admit-22-05-2026-11-
 18-02
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:'Real Vermonters Don’t Milk Goats' 43rd Anniversary Edition Tour
DTSTART:20260920T180000
DTEND:20260920T200000
DTSTAMP:20260920T144436Z
UID:b92def2bb5383d5985f777245fe60f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Real Vermonters Don't Milk Goats is a best-selling book of hum
 or by Frank M. Bryan and the late Bill Mares. Originally published in 1983
 \, the book satirizes the "authentic" Vermont identity by contrasting nati
 ve Vermonters with newcomers (or "flatlanders") through witty observations
  and illustrations by Howard Johnson. Bryan and Mares poke fun at the idea
  of a pure\, unchanging Vermont\, suggesting that "real" Vermonters are de
 fined by their skepticism and a certain kind of self-deprecating humor. It
  was published only a year after the best-seller\, Real Men Don’t Eat Qu
 iche \, took the country by storm. In 2026\, Goats celebrates its 43rd ann
 iversary with a special edition that retains its 1983 hilarity but also of
 fers “explainers” for readers who can’t quite remember the cast of c
 haracters\, or those who moved to Vermont sometime in the last 43 years\, 
 or those who just weren’t born yet. Join us for a fun evening of celebra
 tion. Co-hosted by Don Hooper\, one of the original “non-Vermonters” w
 ho came to Vermont specifically to milk goats\, and Brookfield descendant
 \, “Real Vermonter” Al Boright\, producer and star of Vermont’s infa
 mously funny Ground Hog Oprey.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Brookfield Old Town Hall\, 93 Stone Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/real-vermo
 nters-dont-milk-goats-43rd-anniversary-edition-tour-08-09-2026-11-45-28
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sept 20 | The Lonely Days are Gone Community Square Dance - Brando
 n
DTSTART:20260920T160000
DTEND:20260920T180000
DTSTAMP:20260920T144436Z
UID:b193014cc3f7dde3dcd45619787efe@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:FROM IDA MAE SPECKER & SARAH GIBSON: ‘THE LONELY DAYS ARE GO
 NE’ STATEWIDE SQUARE DANCE TOUR This fall\, ‘The Lonely Days Are Gone:
  Community Square Dance Tour’ brings free concerts and square dances to 
 historic town halls across Vermont. Inspired by the state's long tradition
  of contra and square dancing\, the tour welcomes neighbors of all ages to
  connect through live music\, participatory dancing\, and shared meals. Th
 e tour is headlined by Dorset fiddler\, singer\, and educator Ida Mae Spec
 ker\, alongside Shrewsbury caller Sarah Gibson and The Ida Mae Specker Ban
 d. The Lonely Days Are Gone visits Brandon\, Brookfield\, Hardwick\, Ferri
 sburgh\, and Chester throughout September and October. Participants will l
 earn the basics of square dancing followed by an evening of traditional Am
 erican string band music and dancing with Ida Mae Specker and her all-star
  band. No prior dance experience or partner is required. In addition to da
 nces\, tour stops include special events such as concerts for children and
  old-time music jams. All events are free and open to the public\, and fam
 ilies are encouraged to attend. The tour is part of the nationwide commemo
 ration of America's 250th anniversary\, highlighting the important role th
 at music\, dance\, and town halls have played in civic life throughout New
  England. The Lonely Days Are Gone Tour is supported by Vermont Humanities
 \, the New England Foundation for the Arts and generous individual donors
 \, with media support from Vermont Public. The tour is fiscally sponsored 
 by The Chandler Music Hall in Randolph\, Vermont. Brandon Town Hall\n\nSou
 rces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/sept-20-th
 e-lonely-days-are-gone-community-square-dance-brandon-11-09-2026-14-15-19
END:VEVENT
