BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Words Out Loud: Vievee Francis and Matthew Olzmann
DTSTART:20260920T150000
DTEND:20260920T160000
DTSTAMP:20260920T144436Z
UID:47b282aec56f5a964058924b22dd40@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Words Out Loud As part of event offerings for Art at the Kent
 ’s 2026 exhibit Throughlines at the Kents’ Corner State Historic Site
 \, Words Out Loud\, the popular Sunday afternoon fall reading series\, ret
 urns to the Old West Church. For this year’s second of three readings\, 
 Words Out Loud: Don’t Forget to Write\, welcomes Vermont poets Vievee Fr
 ancis and Matthew Olzmann. To say “Don’t Forget to Write” is to remi
 nd travelers to “stay in touch\,” to "send word" from afar\, wherever 
 they are. This year’s authors remember to write\, and they do so creativ
 ely and intelligently in poetry. Readings will be followed by receptions d
 own the road at the Kent amidst the art on display for this year’s exhib
 it “Throughlines” where attendees may meet and chat with the authors a
 nd a selection of books will be available in the shop. The Words Out Loudr
 eadings take place at the Old West Church at 3:00 p.m. Guests should arriv
 e early to allow time for parking and seating at this historic 200-year-ol
 d meetinghouse in rural Calais\, bring layers for warmth\, and leave pets 
 at home. Open to all. Donations welcome at the door. With a few steps up i
 nto the vestibule\, the historic Old West Church is not ADA accessible at 
 this time. Words Out Loud 2026 has been organized by poet Mary Elder Jacob
 sen with the support of the Art at the Kent curatorial team.\n\nSources: V
 ermont Public
LOCATION:Old West Church\, 758 Old West Church Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/words-out-
 loud-vievee-francis-and-matthew-olzmann-28-08-2026-15-57-56
END:VEVENT
